                                        "dateOnIndeed": 1747921776331,
                                        "description": {
                                            "__typename": "JobDescription",
                                            "html": "\u003Cdiv>\u003Ch2 class=\"jobSectionHeader\">\u003Cb>Frontend Staff Software Engineer\n\u003C\u002Fb>\u003C\u002Fh2>A rapidly growing AI-driven SaaS company is looking for an experienced \u003Cb>Frontend Staff Software Engineer\u003C\u002Fb> to take a strategic and hands-on role in shaping the technical direction of their customer-facing product suite. This role plays a critical part in driving architectural decisions, mentoring team members, and enhancing the performance and reliability of the frontend ecosystem.\n\u003Ch2 class=\"jobSectionHeader\">\u003Cb>Job Description - Frontend Staff Software Engineer\n\u003C\u002Fb>\u003C\u002Fh2>Join a company revolutionizing the contact center space by combining natural language processing and machine learning to deliver automated, conversational customer service across multiple channels.\u003Cp>\nYou will join a high-performing engineering team focused on developing scalable and intelligent user interfaces. This role plays a critical part in driving architectural decisions, mentoring team members, and enhancing the performance and reliability of the frontend ecosystem.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003Cb>\nKey Responsibilities\u003C\u002Fb>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\nDefine and lead the technical roadmap within your domain.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\nInfluence high-level architectural decisions and ensure alignment with broader engineering goals.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\nInitiate and drive improvements in scalability, performance, and developer experience.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\nPromote a culture of continuous learning, quality, and innovation across teams.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\nIdentify technical gaps and propose solutions to enhance frontend capabilities.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\nAdvocate for engineering best practices including accessibility, testing, and observability.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\nCollaborate cross-functionally with product, design, and backend teams to deliver seamless solutions.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\nTrack and improve Service Level Objectives (SLOs) to maintain high standards of system reliability.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\nMentor junior and mid-level engineers, fostering a collaborative and growth-oriented environment.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\n\u003Ch2 class=\"jobSectionHeader\">\u003Cb>Requirements - Frontend Staff Software Engineer\n\u003C\u002Fb>\u003C\u002Fh2>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>Experience as a Staff Software Engineer (or related role), ideally with 4+ years in a senior technical leadership role.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\nDemonstrated ownership of projects that span teams or domains.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\nDeep expertise in modern frontend technologies such as React, Next.js, and TypeScript.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\nStrong understanding of architectural principles for building scalable and maintainable applications.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\nProficiency in HTML, SCSS, and a strong commitment to accessibility and design standards.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\nExperience with API integration (REST, GraphQL) and building intuitive data flows.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\nSkilled in frontend testing tools and methodologies (Playwright, Cypress, Jest, etc.).\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\nAdept at leveraging product analytics to generate actionable insights.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\nComfortable working in agile, high-growth environments with strong collaboration skills.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\nPassion for mentoring, knowledge sharing, and building a thriving engineering culture.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\n\u003Ch2 class=\"jobSectionHeader\">\u003Cb>The offer - Frontend Staff Software Engineer\n\u003C\u002Fb>\u003C\u002Fh2>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>Join a diverse, international team with a strong engineering culture.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\nThe opportunity to shape a product with global impact at the forefront of AI and automation.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\nA base salary of 130-170K plus equity package.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\nFlexible hybrid working model with a modern office in Berlin.\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003C\u002Fdiv>\n\u003Cbr>\n&euro;150000",
                                            "text": "Frontend Staff Software Engineer\nA rapidly growing AI-driven SaaS company is looking for an experienced Frontend Staff Software Engineer to take a strategic and hands-on role in shaping the technical direction of their customer-facing product suite. This role plays a critical part in driving architectural decisions, mentoring team members, and enhancing the performance and reliability of the frontend ecosystem.\nJob Description - Frontend Staff Software Engineer\nJoin a company revolutionizing the contact center space by combining natural language processing and machine learning to deliver automated, conversational customer service across multiple channels.\n\nYou will join a high-performing engineering team focused on developing scalable and intelligent user interfaces. This role plays a critical part in driving architectural decisions, mentoring team members, and enhancing the performance and reliability of the frontend ecosystem.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\nDefine and lead the technical roadmap within your domain.\nInfluence high-level architectural decisions and ensure alignment with broader engineering goals.\nInitiate and drive improvements in scalability, performance, and developer experience.\nPromote a culture of continuous learning, quality, and innovation across teams.\nIdentify technical gaps and propose solutions to enhance frontend capabilities.\nAdvocate for engineering best practices including accessibility, testing, and observability.\nCollaborate cross-functionally with product, design, and backend teams to deliver seamless solutions.\nTrack and improve Service Level Objectives (SLOs) to maintain high standards of system reliability.\nMentor junior and mid-level engineers, fostering a collaborative and growth-oriented environment.\nRequirements - Frontend Staff Software Engineer\nExperience as a Staff Software Engineer (or related role), ideally with 4+ years in a senior technical leadership role.\nDemonstrated ownership of projects that span teams or domains.\nDeep expertise in modern frontend technologies such as React, Next.js, and TypeScript.\nStrong understanding of architectural principles for building scalable and maintainable applications.\nProficiency in HTML, SCSS, and a strong commitment to accessibility and design standards.\nExperience with API integration (REST, GraphQL) and building intuitive data flows.\nSkilled in frontend testing tools and methodologies (Playwright, Cypress, Jest, etc.).\nAdept at leveraging product analytics to generate actionable insights.\nComfortable working in agile, high-growth environments with strong collaboration skills.\nPassion for mentoring, knowledge sharing, and building a thriving engineering culture.\nThe offer - Frontend Staff Software Engineer\nJoin a diverse, international team with a strong engineering culture.\nThe opportunity to shape a product with global impact at the forefront of AI and automation.\nA base salary of 130-170K plus equity package.\nFlexible hybrid working model with a modern office in Berlin.\n\n€150000",
